cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Structure and Computability of the Single-Quadratic Existential Fragment over the Integers (Lean 4 formalization)"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 development accompanying a classification of the total functions definable over the integers
  by one polynomial equation of total degree at most two, with arbitrarily many integer unknowns. The
  forward directions of the classification take the ternary-coset representation input TCER as an
  explicit hypothesis. The development also contains the injective-dimension theorem n <= m, which uses
  no analytic input, the converse constructions, the classification without unknowns, a function that
  needs exactly one unknown in this format, the uniform finite-fibre bounds, the structured
  infinite-fibre theorem, and the computability phase diagrams under two named classical hypotheses.
  The literature-to-TCER adapter is supplied in ordinary mathematics, not as a Lean proof of TCER.
